# covgap_dev_barrier_waiter_above_count_dies: A barrier wait records the waiting FIFO's stamp index, and DeviceCore::add_wait asserts it is below maxFIFOCount, which the version sets (32 below 61, 64 from it) while a child's stamp index is checked against it only at its creation. Children 1 and 2, with stamp indices 31 and 32, are created at version 245; the guest then writes version 60. Child 1 (31) blocks on root slot 0 (a 300 ms wait that times out is the behaviour) and a root NOP releases it. Child 2 (32) then waits on the root slot too: the assert fails (32 < 32 is false) and the host dies at the wait.
